        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: વિરહ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વિરહ — virah — \"the pain of separation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પતિ દૂર ગયો છે, તેથી પત્નીને વિરહનું દુઃખ છે. pati dūr gayo che, tethī patnīne virahnũ duḥkh che. Her husband has gone far away, so the wife suffers the pain of separation."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વિરહ (virah) is a tatsama, Sanskrit viraha, \"abandonment, parting, separation, especially of lovers\", as Monier-Williams records it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
